      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SIMPLY SID (3) looks the goods in a moderate maiden. Settled midfield then wound up strongly to grab second when resuming over this course and distance two weeks ago. Still to win after 14 runs but this is as good a chance as he has ever had. NOLABELL (9) has not appeared since finishing down the track in the Listed Dequetteville at Morphettville in March at her only run to date. The stable must hold an opinion of the filly to throw her in the deep end on debut. Should go well with two recent jump-outs under the belt. LARRY CAN (2) made a midrace move after a poor start then tired late on debut over 1100m at Murray Bridge recently. Can play a major role if he jumps a bit better. BLAZING MISSILE (5) raced handy then battled on okay for a distant third over this course and distance a fortnight ago. Open to further improvement at just his third race start. Recent jump-out winner CHARLES BRIDGE (6) is coming along nicely for the Jolly stable and should give a good account on debut.",
